		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Undead figure, featureless face like wet clay. Tricks mortals and drains them.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 13, <strong>HP</strong> 21, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 touch +3 (1d4 + will drain), <strong>MV</strong> near (fly), <strong>S</strong> +3, <strong>D</strong> +3, <strong>C</strong> +3, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> +1, <strong>Ch</strong> +3, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 4</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Appearance</strong>. Appears as the mortal it was in life.</p><p></p><p><strong>Greater Undead</strong>. Immune to morale checks. Only damaged by silver or magical sources.</p><p></p><p><strong>Rejuvenation</strong>. If destroyed, reforms in 2d4 days unless hupia's body is burned.</p><p></p><p><strong>Will Drain</strong>. WIS 15+ or lose 1 CHA permanently.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
